# UI Spacing and Layout Consistency

- Prioritize visual rhythm: use consistent vertical spacing between headings, notes, cards, and forms.
- Center single-focus setup flows (e.g., onboarding/auth) with a clear max width and balanced whitespace.
- Avoid awkward split headers where helper text is detached or misaligned; keep subtitle/support text visually grouped with its heading.
- For every UI change, review nearby elements (header, body copy, controls, empty space, alignment) and optimize the whole section, not only one node.
- Keep typography hierarchy explicit: strong headline font, readable body size, muted helper text, and consistent line-height.
- Ensure responsive behavior preserves spacing quality on narrow widths (no crowded controls or drifting helper text).
